    "created_at": "2025-07-18T18:17:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-29T18:47:12Z",
    "body": "I think the default should be to accept immutable buffers. Even for APIs which write to their argument (which are rare - TextEncoder encodeInto comes to mind, but little else) they'll just throw when they actually try to write. [Edit: actually no, since they manipulate things internally, some algorithms would need to be updated I'm sure.]\n\nIt would be nice for APIs which do a copy to be updated not to do that, but this is an unobservable optimization which engines could do anyway, so it's not strictly necessary.\n\nMaybe instead there should be a `[ForbidImmutable]` attribute for the those rare cases?",
